{
  "name": "318. MiniMax base_resp errors carry error_type; vendor-caused codes return 502 (minimax base resp)",
  "description": "Contract C6 for MiniMax (TXE-6588): MiniMax answers its failures inside an HTTP 200 as base_resp{status_code, status_msg} with no result. Bifrost returns an error: a vendor cause (key, balance, rate limit, timeout, server fault) is a 502 with a provider_* error_type, a customer cause (parameters, content filtering 1026/1027) is a 400, and error.code is MiniMax's code verbatim. The fixture's /pp/minimax routes answer chat, speech, image generation and video create with the base_resp code named by the model (base-resp-<code>), and video query with the code named by the task id; /v1/responses reaches MiniMax's chat path. Before TXE-6588 rows 1-3 came back as 401, 402 and 429, rows 4-5 as caller_invalid_request, rows 7, 9 and 10 as 402, 429 and 401, and rows 8 and 11 as caller_invalid_request; row 6 is unchanged. The cases run only against the provider error fixture (providerErrorFixture=1).",
  "item": [
    {
      "name": "318.1 [EXPECT-502] /v1/chat/completions - base_resp 1004 (invalid key) in a 200 is a 502 provider_auth_failed (minimax base resp)",
      "request": {
        "method": "POST",
        "header": [
          {
            "key": "Content-Type",
            "value": "application/json"
          }
        ],
        "body": {
          "mode": "raw",
          "raw": "{\n  \"model\": \"minimax/base-resp-1004\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"hi\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"max_tokens\": 8\n}"
        },
        "url": {
          "raw": "{{baseUrl}}/v1/chat/completions",
          "host": [
            "{{baseUrl}}"
          ],
          "path": [
            "v1",
            "chat",
            "completions"
          ]
        }
      },
      "event": [
        {
          "listen": "prerequest",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "if (pm.variables.get('providerErrorFixture') !== '1') {",
              "  pm.execution.skipRequest();",
              "}"
            ]
          }
        },
        {
          "listen": "test",
          "script": {
            "type": "text/javascript",
            "exec": [
              "pm.test('a vendor-caused base_resp code is a 502 with a provider_* error_type', function () {",
              "  pm.expect(pm.response.code, 'status: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql(502);",
              "  var j = pm.response.json();",
              "  pm.expect(j.extra_fields && j.extra_fields.error_type, 'error_type: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('provider_auth_failed');",
              "  pm.expect(j.error && j.error.code, 'vendor code: ' + pm.response.text()).to.eql('1004');",
              "});"
            ]
          }
        }
      ]
    },
